---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { emailTestingDescription, sampleEmail } from "../lib/email-testing";
import { engineVersion } from "../lib/playground";
import clientsPackage from "../../../../packages/email-clients/package.json";
import "../styles/email-testing.css";

const cli = `npx @hyper-elements/cli check email.html --json
npx @hyper-elements/cli preview email.html`;
const library = `import { mkdir, readFile, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
import { renderInEmailClients } from "@hyper-elements/email-clients";

const html = await readFile("email.html", "utf8");
const { previews, diagnostics } = await renderInEmailClients(html, {
  emailClients: ["outlook", "gmail", "apple-mail"],
});

await mkdir("out", { recursive: true });
for (const preview of previews) {
  await writeFile(\`out/\${preview.filename}\`, preview.html);
}
console.log(diagnostics);`;
const agent = `await window.hyperElementsEmailTesting.check({
  html: "<!doctype html><html><body>…</body></html>",
  clients: ["outlook", "gmail", "apple-mail"],
  dark: false,
});`;
---
<Base title="Test HTML emails across email clients" description={emailTestingDescription} footer={false}>
  <section id="playground" class="et-workspace" aria-labelledby="playground-title" data-email-testing data-mobile-pane="preview" data-runtime-version={`${engineVersion}-${clientsPackage.version}-html-3`}>
    <header class="et-topbar">
      <div class="et-heading"><h1 id="playground-title">Email playground</h1><span class="et-local"><i></i> Runs locally</span></div>
      <div class="et-top-actions">
        <button class="et-subtle" id="email-help-open" type="button">Library &amp; help</button>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="email-open" type="button" disabled>Open HTML</button>
        <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="email-export" type="button" disabled>Export HTML <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
        <input id="email-file" type="file" accept=".html,.htm,text/html" hidden />
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="et-mobile-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Workspace panel">
      <button type="button" role="tab" data-mobile-tab="edit" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="email-editor-panel">HTML</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" data-mobile-tab="preview" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="email-preview-panel">Preview</button>
    </div>

    <div class="et-bench">
      <section class="et-input" id="email-editor-panel" aria-label="Email editor">
        <div class="et-editor-bar"><label for="email-html">email.html</label><label class="et-live"><input id="email-live" type="checkbox" checked /> Live preview</label></div>
        <div class="et-code surface-dark" id="email-code">
          <div class="et-code-caption"><span>HTML</span><button type="button" id="email-example" class="et-subtle" disabled>Load example</button></div>
          <textarea id="email-html" aria-describedby="email-input-help" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocomplete="off" wrap="off">{sampleEmail}</textarea>
          <p id="email-input-help">Complete HTML · Up to 250 KB · ⌘ / Ctrl + Enter to preview</p>
        </div>
        <div class="et-editor-footer"><span>HTML stays in this tab</span><button type="button" id="email-run" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" disabled>Update preview ↵</button></div>
      </section>

      <section class="et-output" id="email-preview-panel" aria-label="Email preview">
        <div class="et-output-bar">
          <div><button type="button" id="email-all" class="et-subtle" hidden>← All clients</button><h2 id="email-view-title">Client previews <span id="email-client-count"></span></h2></div>
          <label class="et-dark"><input id="email-dark" type="checkbox" /> Dark mode</label>
        </div>
        <div class="et-preview-controls" id="email-preview-controls" hidden>
          <label class="et-sr-only" for="email-preview">Choose a client preview</label><select id="email-preview" disabled></select>
          <span class="et-preview-spacer"></span>
          <button type="button" id="email-details" class="et-subtle" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Render details</button>
          <button type="button" id="email-size" class="et-subtle" disabled>Actual size</button>
        </div>
        <div class="et-canvas">
          <div class="et-empty" id="email-empty"><span class="et-loading" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2>Your email, across clients.</h2><p>Preparing client previews…</p></div>
          <div class="et-gallery" id="email-gallery" aria-label="Email client thumbnails" hidden></div>
          <div class="et-viewport" id="email-viewport" hidden><div id="email-sheet"></div></div>
          <p id="email-error" class="et-notice" role="alert" hidden></p>
        </div>
        <div class="et-canvas-footer"><span id="email-preview-note">Modeled email preview</span><span>Images and fonts may load from their hosts</span></div>
        <details class="et-findings" id="email-findings" hidden>
          <summary><span>Compatibility <span id="email-findings-count" class="et-count">0</span></span><span class="et-findings-prompt">Review findings ⌃</span></summary>
          <div class="et-findings-content"><p id="email-findings-summary"></p><ul id="email-diagnostics"></ul><ul id="email-skipped" class="et-skipped"></ul><button type="button" class="et-subtle" id="email-download" disabled>Download report ↓</button></div>
        </details>
      </section>
    </div>
    <div class="et-status-bar"><p id="email-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading the example…</p><a href="/docs/email-client-emulator">Client coverage &amp; accuracy ↗</a></div>
    <noscript><p class="et-notice">Enable JavaScript to edit HTML and preview emails, or use the <a href="/docs/cli">CLI</a>.</p></noscript>
  </section>

  <dialog id="email-help" class="et-help" aria-labelledby="help-title">
    <header><h2 id="help-title">Email testing, in your workflow</h2><form method="dialog"><button class="et-subtle" aria-label="Close help">✕</button></form></header>
    <div class="et-help-body">
      <p>Paste or edit a complete HTML email on the left. Compare the client thumbnails on the right, then click a client to open its full preview. Use All clients to return to the overview. Preview Outlook, Gmail, Apple Mail, Yahoo Mail and AOL Mail locally. HTML from any builder, MJML, or React Email works here.</p>
      <p>Live preview updates after you pause typing. Export HTML downloads your email; Download report saves compatibility diagnostics. Your HTML is not uploaded or saved as a draft. Referenced images and fonts may load from their hosts.</p>
      <p>These are modeled previews. Some variants are approximate, and a clean report does not guarantee identical rendering in every inbox. Use <strong>Render details</strong> to see what changed, missing assets, and browser findings for the selected preview. <a href="/docs/email-client-emulator#checks-and-the-emulator">How the checks and emulator work.</a></p>
      <section id="use-in-code"><h3>Use the library or CLI</h3><p>No React or test send is needed for HTML input. The CLI also adds readability checks.</p><CodeBlock code={cli} lang="bash" file="Terminal" /><p>Open the generated files under <code>out/clients/email/</code> in Chromium or Chrome. See the <a href="/docs/cli#preview">CLI browser setup</a>.</p><CodeBlock code={library} lang="js" file="preview-email.mjs" /><p>Install <code>@hyper-elements/email-clients</code>, run the example with Node, and open <code>out/outlook.html</code>. See the <a href="/docs/email-client-emulator#test-any-html-email">HTML email API</a>.</p></section>
      <section><h3>For browser agents</h3><p>Use <code>window.hyperElementsEmailTesting.check()</code> or the WebMCP <code>check_html_email</code> tool where supported. Both update the workspace and return diagnostics, preview metadata, and skipped variants. <code>ok</code> means generation succeeded; inspect diagnostics and approximate flags before judging compatibility.</p><CodeBlock code={agent} lang="js" /><p>Client IDs: <code>outlook</code>, <code>outlook-com</code>, <code>gmail</code>, <code>gmail-app</code>, <code>apple-mail</code>, <code>yahoo</code>, <code>aol</code>. Omit them to use Outlook, Gmail and Apple Mail.</p></section>
    </div>
  </dialog>
  <script>
    import "../email-testing/main";
  </script>
</Base>
